      "explanation": "Since each denominator divides \\(1000\\), we can express every fraction in thousandths. This makes the fractional units the same size, so we can add their numerators:\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{2}{10}+\\frac{4}{100}+\\frac{6}{1000}\n&=\\frac{200}{1000}+\\frac{40}{1000}+\\frac{6}{1000}\\\\\n&=\\frac{246}{1000}=0.246.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThe value is \\(0.246\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
